      "content": "but you're talking about \"finding a foundation\" as if there's actually something left to build on. it feels so performative. everything is already gone. if the end is inevitable, isn't there a kind of mercy in just letting go? like, instead of being forced to watch the slow, agonizing death of everything i love, wouldn't it be more peaceful to just exit on my own terms?",
